 "notes": "Dark photon dark matter kinetic mixing epsilon (=chi) bound. Curve taken directly from the e-print ancillary file anc/DarkPhoton_DM_Constraint_Summary_Inhomogeneous_Combined.dat (col1=m_A in eV, col2=epsilon), which is the papers own combined constraint from Lyman-alpha forest observations of HeII reionization (resonant conversion, Fig.4 left, plus non-resonant inverse-bremsstrahlung absorption, Fig.4 right) in their inhomogeneous treatment. This is the headline measured limit; the 21cm results (Sec.4) are projections and excluded. Reported chi directly (not chi^2). Text cross-check: min epsilon ~ 1.75e-15 near m_A ~ 3-6e-14... resonant min quoted as extension of Ref [21] epsilon<2e-15. Points with col2=1 (no constraint, m<2.5e-22 eV) dropped. Limit assumes dark photon is 100% of cosmological dark matter; depends on cosmological rho_CDM(z), not a local halo density, so dm_density_assumed=null. CMB grey region in Fig.4 is borrowed from Ref [21] and not included. Confidence level not explicitly stated by the paper (Ly-alpha heating bound <=0.5 eV/baryon); 0.95 assumed.",
